# Build output. `dist/easyvm` is produced by the workflow's first job and copied into the image;
# it is never committed, because a binary in a repository is a binary nobody rebuilds.
/dist/

# A run's scratch: frames, disks and recordings. The daemon defaults its work directory to the
# walkthrough's own directory, so these can land anywhere.
*.qcow2
*.qcow2.part
*.mp4
*.ppm
*.sock

# Editors.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
# THE BUILT BINARY IS NAMED `easyvm`, AND A BARE PATTERN FOR IT ALSO MATCHES THE PACKAGE DIRECTORY
# `cmd/easyvm/` - so a NEW FILE THERE WAS SILENTLY IGNORED. MEASURED: `cmd/easyvm/walk.go` was written,
# built, tested locally and absent from the commit, and CI answered
#
#	cmd/easyvm/main.go:85:11: undefined: cmdWalk
#
# The slash anchors it to a file in the root, which is what a build output is.
/easyvm
__pycache__/
